{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04DJ", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$X_\\etale$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$X_\\etale$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{W_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0006": "$X_\\etale$", "MATH_0007": "$W_i$", "MATH_0008": "$X \\times_Y V_i$", "MATH_0009": "$V_i$", "MATH_0010": "$Y_\\etale$", "MATH_0011": "$$\n\\mathcal{F}(U) \\subset \\prod \\mathcal{F}(W_i)\n$$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{F}(W_i)$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{F}(X \\times_Y V_i) = f_{small, *}\\mathcal{F}(V_i)$", "MATH_0014": "$f_{small, *}$", "MATH_0015": "$a : \\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0016": "$f_{small, *}a$", "MATH_0017": "$s \\in \\mathcal{F}(U)$", "MATH_0018": "$U$", "MATH_0019": "$W_i$", "MATH_0020": "$V_i$", "MATH_0021": "$s|_{W_i}$", "MATH_0022": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0023": "$a$", "MATH_0024": "$\\mathcal{F}(W_i)$", "MATH_0025": "$\\mathcal{F}(X \\times_Y V_i)$", "MATH_0026": "$V \\in \\Ob(Y_\\etale)$", "MATH_0027": "$s \\in \\mathcal{F}(X \\times_Y V)$", "MATH_0028": "$X \\times_Y V$", "MATH_0029": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0030": "$a$", "MATH_0031": "$\\mathcal{F}(X \\times_Y V) = f_{small, *}\\mathcal{F}(V)$", "MATH_0032": "$\\{V_j \\to V\\}$", "MATH_0033": "$s$", "MATH_0034": "$s_j \\in f_{small, *}\\mathcal{G}(V_j) = \\mathcal{G}(X \\times_Y V_j)$", "MATH_0035": "$f_{small, *}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-reflect-surjections}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0003": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0004": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7b414e0d441dc81891dbcf2e0e949fc3f0f79f06c22197fd0eb65c5ac55c16da", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2e94efe16d4df37593c7cb761419561c4b1533b35c601d571a741509efac8642", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an abelian sheaf on <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be an object of <MATH_0004>. By assumption we can find a\ncovering <MATH_0005> in <MATH_0006> such that each <MATH_0007> is\nan open and closed subscheme of <MATH_0008> for some object\n<MATH_0009> of <MATH_0010>. The sheaf condition shows that\n<MATH_0011>\nand that <MATH_0012> is a direct summand of\n<MATH_0013>.\nHence it is clear that <MATH_0014> reflects injections.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nNext, suppose that <MATH_0015> is a map of\nabelian sheaves such that <MATH_0016> is surjective. Let\n<MATH_0017> with <MATH_0018> as above. With <MATH_0019>, <MATH_0020> as\nabove we see that it suffices to show that <MATH_0021> is <ACCENT_0001>tale locally\nthe image of a section of <MATH_0022> under <MATH_0023>. Since <MATH_0024>\nis a direct summand of <MATH_0025>\nit suffices to show that for any <MATH_0026>\nany element <MATH_0027>\nis <ACCENT_0002>tale locally on <MATH_0028> the image of a section of\n<MATH_0029> under <MATH_0030>. Since\n<MATH_0031>\nwe see by assumption that there exists a covering <MATH_0032> such that\n<MATH_0033> is the image of\n<MATH_0034>.\nThis proves <MATH_0035> reflects surjections.\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nParts (2), (3) follow formally from part (1), see\nModules on Sites, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b6ebc3be094581a081e475c7f0f010ad15d1fab2466e9e69c0e0d82c29841cbe", "unit_id": "tag:04DK:proof"}
